media: qcom: camss: Two sensors on one CSIPHY

The Moto G Power (2021) has its macro and depth cameras on one CSIPHY, in the mode where lanes 0 and 1
form one link and lanes 2 and 3 another. Both work with these patches, one at a time.

This is an RFC because of how it's modelled, which is the simplest thing that works: two endpoints on
the port, ordinary links from the sensors to the CSIPHY's one sink pad, and only one enabled at a
time. Streaming from both at once needs more than that, likely streams and routing on the CSIPHY, and
may want a different starting point. It also doesn't touch the new PHY API mode.
